---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Where the pickers of the settings take their names from
    accDescr: The field of the target user asks Paperless Sync for the users of Nextcloud whose ID, name or e-mail address holds what is typed, and for the user ID that the field names, which it marks when Nextcloud has no such user. The fields of the excluded tags, the tags to mirror and the tags for every import ask Paperless Sync, which reads the tags from Paperless-ngx with the stored URL and API token, as a run does; the token stays on the server. A name that Paperless has no tag of can be added too, and is marked as not in Paperless.

    page(["Settings page in the<br>browser of an administrator"])
    subgraph nextcloud ["Nextcloud server"]
        users["Paperless Sync:<br>the users of Nextcloud"]
        app["Paperless Sync:<br>the tags of Paperless"]
    end
    paperless[("Paperless-ngx")]

    page -- "`target user:<br>users that match,<br>*an unknown ID is marked*`" --> users
    page -- "`excluded tags,<br>tags to mirror and<br>tags for every import:<br>names to pick,<br>*a new name is marked*`" --> app
    app -- "`the stored URL and token,<br>as a run reads them;<br>*the token stays on the server*`" --> paperless

    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    class paperless paperless
    class users,app nextcloud
